# Stations for ~/.local/bin/focus-music. One per line: a name, a TAB, a URL.
#
# Tracked here rather than inside the helper, so adding a station is editing
# data rather than editing a script - and so a rebuilt machine has the same
# list. Comments and blank lines are ignored.
#
# THE NAMES LEAD WITH THE SOUND, NOT THE BRAND
#
# "Fluid" and "Lush" tell you nothing at the moment you are choosing, which is
# the only moment the name is read. The descriptor comes first and the station
# name follows it, so the list can be skimmed for a mood and still says where
# each one came from. rofi matches anywhere in the line, so typing "lush" or
# "dub" both still find them.
#
# WHY DIRECT AUDIO URLS
#
# No yt-dlp, no API, no key, and no resolving step that can break independently
# of the player - every URL below was checked returning audio before being
# written down. A YouTube live stream needs resolving on every start and its
# video id changes whenever the channel restarts, which turns a station into a
# thing that stops working for reasons nobody can see.
#
# yt-dlp is still declared, so pasting a YouTube or SoundCloud link here works.
# It is just not what the defaults depend on.
#
# SomaFM is listener-supported and serves no ads: https://somafm.com/support/
# Their channel list, with ids for the URL pattern below, is at
# https://somafm.com/channels.json

